## 3. `mcp` ships TWICE, at two different versions

Both are distributed, so both are recorded. This is not a duplicate entry to be
cleaned up:

| Component | Version | License | Why this version |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `index-service` | 1.23.3 | MIT | Deliberate exact pin in `index-service/requirements.txt`, protocol-verified against `codegraph-server` 0.18.5. Bumping it risks the stdio/FastMCP contract with the index engine. |
| `agent-container` | 1.28.0 | MIT | Transitive. `claude-agent-sdk==0.2.103` requires `mcp>=1.23.0,<2.0.0` (read from its wheel metadata); `requirements.lock` froze whatever that range resolved to in the verified ARM64 build. |

The divergence is intentional and safe because the two never share an
interpreter: `index-service` runs on the EC2 index host, `agent-container` runs
in the AgentCore microVM, and they talk over HTTP. Anyone raising the
index-service pin must re-verify against `codegraph-server`; anyone changing the
agent-container version must rebuild and re-freeze the lock.

Same pattern, lower stakes: `uvicorn` ships at 0.44.0 (index-service, pinned)
and 0.49.0 (agent-container, transitive).

